.AVIATION...
(12Z TAFS)
Issued at 432 AM PDT Sat Aug 15 2026

A deep marine layer is bringing widespread stratus to all Bay Area
and Monterey Peninsula Airports. Highest confidence in MVFR CIGs
with IFR across the North Bay Valleys and along the coast.
Ensembles show a decent chance for clearing between 17-18Z but the
deeper/substantial marine layer typically takes longer to clear
than models expect so I kept the the later clearing times in the
TAFs (18-20Z). The biggest tweak was to MRY where I added in a
brief period of VFR conditions this afternoon before an early
return of stratus. MVFR-IFR CIGs are expected again tonight.
Diurnally breezy onshore winds continue with lighter winds
overnight.

Vicinity of SFO...MVFR CIGs with drizzle through late morning.
LAMP probabilistic guidance shows a low chance for IFR CIGs this
morning but confidence is low that CIGs will drop below 1000 feet.
Stratus clears between 18-20Z with VFR then persisting through the
evening. Stratus returns late evening/overnight and persists
through the remainder of the TAF period.

SFO Bridge Approach...Similar to SFO.

Monterey Bay Terminals...MVFR with IFR CIGs to at least
temporarily develop this morning. Highest confidence in IFR CIGs
impacting MRY over SNS but it cannot be fully ruled out there.
Went slightly more optimistic for the MRY TAF and included a brief
period of VFR this afternoon. Ensembles were more optimistic that
cloud cover would recede along the coast and HRRR guidance
suggested reductions in humidity (proxy for cloud cover) starting
around 20Z. Regardless, stratus comes back to both sites by the
early evening and persists through the rest of the TAF period.
CIGs initially start out MVFR but are expected to lower to IFR.
Not anticipating LIFR CIGs tonight but with the marine layer
compressing and ridging starting to push in, it may be possible
CIGs lower further than currently expected.

