A gentle to moderate northwesterly breeze persists into early
next week with localized fresh gusts possible across the interior
waters. A long period southerly swell of about 16 to 18 seconds
will linger through Sunday. Winds increase to fresh to strong
early next week and remain elevated through the end of the
forecast period. Seas subside this weekend before building to 7 to
9 feet mid week.

